crau-nbd NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

* Noteworthy changes in release 0.1.0 (2026-09-03) [initial release]

** New features

  - Initial release of crau-nbd: A Linux Network Block Device (NBD) daemon
    for direct, read-only block mounting of partitions inside Android and
    ChromeOS CrAU v2 payload.bin images.
  - Supports zero-scratch direct seeking on uncompressed (Stored) OTA ZIP
    archives, eliminating multi-gigabyte disk extraction.
  - Adheres strictly to IEEE Std 1003.1 (POSIX.1) and GNU Coding Standards.
  - Clean rejection of deflated ZIP containers with diagnostic instructions
    directing users to mount-zip.
  - Multi-threaded streaming decompression for REPLACE_XZ (LZMA), REPLACE_BZ
    (bzip2), and REPLACE (raw extents) with LRU chunk caching.
  - PolicyKit (pkexec) integration for supervised execution on desktop systems.
